1. She became a Twitch partner, marking a significant milestone in her streaming career. (Verbatim: "I hit Twitch partner today. Yippee!")

2. This was her second attempt at achieving Twitch partnership. (Verbatim: "But, yeah! Yeah, that's why I was surprised. I was like, second try? Eh, really?")

3. She attended VExpo, the first VTuber convention in Europe, held in England. (Verbatim: "I have been at VExpo, which is a VTuber convention in England. The first, the first. I believe it's the first in Europe.")

4. She is based in the UK and identifies as a British streamer. (Verbatim: "I've moved on with my life. I found other anime girls." — referring to being a "weird British punk")

5. She has been streaming for at least several months and has content planned through the next year. (Verbatim: "I've got stuff planned out for next year, like through to like, at least this time next year already planned out.")

6. She plans to release original songs as part of her future content. (Verbatim: "For example, you know, new outfits, 3D model, um, original songs, um, all sorts, all sorts, all sorts.")

7. She is working on a 3D model for her channel. (Verbatim: "For example, you know, new outfits, 3D model, um, original songs...")

8. She expresses a strong commitment to long-term content creation and community growth. (Verbatim: "Don't worry, I'm here for a long time, I'm here for a long, long, long time.")

9. She enjoys chatting with her audience and considers it one of her favorite activities as a streamer. (Verbatim: "We're gonna be yapping, yapping, because that's what I do best. That's what I enjoy.")

10. She initially doubted receiving Twitch partnership and thought the email might be a glitch. (Verbatim: "I looked at it and I was like, nah, nah me. There's no way that's true. No. So I didn't actually tweet right away.") [end of text]



1. She worked at a zoo for a period of time. (Verbatim: "i worked at a zoo for a bit um rest in peace little dogs rest in peace")  
2. She has a fondness for prairie dogs and once cared for them, though they all died after being eaten by a bird of prey. (Verbatim: "i used to look after prairie dogs for a bit then they all died because they got eaten by a giant bird of prey the end")  
3. She considers herself kind and trusting, but has been told she is naive. (Verbatim: "i try i do try i get told i'm naive quite a lot but that's okay i get told i'm too trusting but i just want to be kind")  
4. She dislikes wearing high heels and finds them painful, especially at conventions. (Verbatim: "heels is um pain i've worn heels to one convention... never wear heels at a convention it hurts for sure")  
5. She has cosplayed as the character Yore twice, learning from experience to wear more comfortable footwear the second time. (Verbatim: "i've dressed as i cosplayed as yore twice now... the second time i learned my lesson and wore thicker thicker boots platform heel things instead")  
6. She enjoys Ritz biscuits and finds them delicious. (Verbatim: "ritz biscuits do you guys have ritz biscuits i really like ritz biscuits they're really yummy")  
7. She attended afternoon tea and described herself as very fancy during the event. (Verbatim: "i went to afternoon tea we had we had yeah i was so fancy we're super fancy")  
8. Her father, "Papa Eliot," is a motorcycle punk with tattoos and a rock/metal background. (Verbatim: "papa elliot is an actual punk like an actual motorcycle punk like tattoo sleeve like rock heavy metal whatever that kind of life")  
9. Her mother, "Mama Elio," likes gothic aesthetics, skulls, and dragons. (Verbatim: "mama elio really likes um she really likes gothic stuff she really likes like dragons and and not dragons like like skulls there's a lot of skulls a lot of souls and dragons")  
10. She felt like an outsider in school, describing herself as a "heckin nerd kid and no friends," and believes her parents would have bullied her if they were students at the same school. (Verbatim: "i think both of them would have bullied me at school um you guys may have i guess i'm the heckin nerd kid and no friends what up") [end of text]



1. Her father (Papa Elia) had a mischievous past involving fire and motorbikes, and was once chased by the police. (Verbatim: "one time papa elia was getting chased by the police and so he ran home and was like please start after me... he just really likes fire fire and motorbikes and i don't know what else tattoos i guess")

2. Her mother (Mama Elia) is extremely cautious about fire, claiming she once accidentally burnt down her house as a child. (Verbatim: "mama elia was always really really really really careful with fire because she said that when she was younger she accidentally knocked over a candle and burnt down her house")

3. Mama Elia may be a compulsive liar, casting doubt on the truthfulness of her stories. (Verbatim: "but she's also a compulsive liar so i don't know if that story is true")

4. She was raised to be very careful around fire due to her mother’s warnings. (Verbatim: "i wasn't allowed near any fire like um")

5. She grew up hearing exaggerated cautionary tales from adults, similar to urban legends meant to scare children. (Verbatim: "have you guys been told stories that are like um don't rock back on your chair there was a kid that did it knocked back and then hit their head and died")

6. She attended church as a child because her grandmother made her go. (Verbatim: "i went to church because my nan made me go to church")

7. Her father once tried to set a church on fire using incense. (Verbatim: "your dad he um he tried to use the incense to set the church on fire")

8. An uncle mentioned that her father once set a field on fire. (Verbatim: "your dad set this all on fire once and i was like ah damn it why")

9. She identifies with British culture and is familiar with British banter. (Verbatim: "i'm british as well like i'm used to british banter i guess")

10. She struggles with social anxiety, often overthinking interactions and worrying about making a bad impression. (Verbatim: "the spiral of yeah am i overthinking the overthinking or am i not thinking enough and i need to think more so i can be more considerate in the future") [end of text]



1. Her name is Elia Stellaria. (Verbatim: "allow me to introduce myself um my name is elia salaria i'm a british vtuber")  
2. She is a British VTuber. (Verbatim: "my name is elia salaria i'm a british vtuber")  
3. She recently became a partnered streamer. (Verbatim: "i hit partner today yippee yippee yippee yippee")  
4. She streams on both YouTube and Twitch, originally starting on YouTube. (Verbatim: "i'm originally from youtube i'm venturing into twitch")  
5. She attended and participated in VXO, Europe’s first VTuber convention, as a guest. (Verbatim: "i went both in person and as a guest um i did a meet and greet and i did two panels")  
6. She has previously attended Anime Expo. (Verbatim: "i had the same thing when i went to like anime expo and stuff")  
7. She wants to perform in concerts and have fan merchandise, including plushies and a booth at conventions. (Verbatim: "i want to be able to sing at a concert you know maybe we'll have my heck and ellie booth with a billion heck and ellie standees")  
8. She is highly ambitious and motivated by a desire to bring happiness despite her spite toward the world. (Verbatim: "i'm very very ambitious but that's because i have a lot of anger towards the world... i'm powered by spite and cola and some ritz biscuits")  
9. She remembers chat usernames well, though she struggles with remembering real-life names. (Verbatim: "i'm really good at remembering names um like in chat names irl for actual people i'm a heckin lost cause")  
10. She drinks Pepsi and prefers Coca-Cola, and enjoys Ritz biscuits. (Verbatim: "they gave me like a like a constant supply of um pepsi which is really sweet even if i'm kokikola person" and "i'm powered by spite and cola and some ritz biscuits") [end of text]



1. She has struggled with severe social anxiety and once couldn't go outside or speak to people. (Verbatim: "there was a time where i couldn't even go outside i people thought i was mute didn't have any friends")

2. She used to practice greeting people by rehearsing in the mirror every morning. (Verbatim: "i used to practice in the mirror like every single morning to be like i'm gonna say hello to somebody today")

3. A past attempt to greet someone resulted in rejection, which made her cry. (Verbatim: "i remember the first time i did manage to go up to someone and say hello... they looked at me and they're like why are you talking to me and then i cried")

4. She identifies as introverted and finds socializing draining, even though she pushes herself to improve. (Verbatim: "i'm not a social person okay i'm full of social anxiety i want to go home and stream and chill with you guys... it does drain me")

5. She prefers streaming and staying home over attending social events like conventions. (Verbatim: "i want to go home and stream and chill with you guys that is straight up what i want to do")

6. She has a strong interest in anime and estimates having watched over 500 full-length anime series. (Verbatim: "i've seen about 500 no just over 500 full-length anime series")

7. She loves shonen rom-com anime such as *Horimiya* and *Kakuya-sama: Love is War*. (Verbatim: "i really like that one that one's great... kakuya sama love is war counts as one of them um and i love those ones")

8. She dislikes drama in real life but can enjoy drama genre anime, though it stresses her. (Verbatim: "i don't i don't drama... even then I get kind of stressed")

9. She finds *Gamers!* anime to be an exaggerated satire of misunderstandings. (Verbatim: "misunderstandings absolute the anime like all it is is misunderstanding piled on top of misunderstanding")

10. She has rewatched *Hunter x Hunter* multiple times, possibly up to seven. (Verbatim: "i could go watch hunter hunter again like for like the seventh time i think i think that's possible") [end of text]



1. She is from England and lives in the south of England. (Verbatim: "i'm british i'm from england i live in the south can confirm")
2. She has a British accent, which influences how her written words are perceived. (Verbatim: "the voice in your head has a british accent a british accent isn't that absolutely fantastic")
3. She associates her writing style with her natural speech, as she no longer writes formal reports. (Verbatim: "i write exactly as i speak because i don't have to write scientific reports anymore so i just i just write directly from the brain")
4. She used to memorize information by recalling her teachers' voices during school exams. (Verbatim: "i used to remember a lot of stuff for class for exams i could remember it from my teacher's voice")
5. She enjoys traditional English afternoon tea and recently attended one with sandwiches, scones, and cakes. (Verbatim: "I went for was what I went for the other day and it was fantastic and I had lots of delicious tiny sandwiches and scones and cute little cakes")
6. She prefers tea over coffee, especially during afternoon tea, and has tried specific blends like royal blend black tea and jasmine-infused silver needle white tea. (Verbatim: "for my second tea I had a white tea infused with jasmine which was like um I think it was called like um silver needle or something")
7. She drank tea from Wedgewood China at a recent afternoon tea event. (Verbatim: "the tea was all served in beautiful Wedgewood China")
8. She finds it culturally significant that in southern England, the evening meal is often called "tea," which can cause confusion. (Verbatim: "meal time late afternoon we will call it tea... it's very confusing because you can still have tea the drink but yeah it's a south thing")
9. Her mother uses American English terms, which has influenced her own speech patterns. (Verbatim: "my mother's quite americanized she uses a lot of american words anyway")
10. She finds it improper or unusual to drink tea with dinner, unlike with breakfast or afternoon tea. (Verbatim: "i'd never have it with the only time i'd have tea the drink with a meal would be like if i was having a full english breakfast with a cup of tea") [end of text]



1. She has been active on YouTube for a significantly longer time than on Twitch. (Verbatim: "it's wild to think i've been with youtube so much longer though than than twitch")

2. She became a Twitch partner after 15 months on the platform. (Verbatim: "thank you happy 15 months damn already 15 months... ellian congratulations for the twitch partnership")

3. She struggles with imposter syndrome but copes by continuing to do her best. (Verbatim: "that's my way of dealing with imposter syndrome just by keep on doing my bestest because that's all that i can do")

4. She has nostalgic memories of playing Professor Layton games and helping her mother solve puzzles. (Verbatim: "i had to help my mother out with playing it i would borrow it and complete the puzzles for her")

5. She was deeply obsessed with Ace Attorney around the same time as playing Professor Layton. (Verbatim: "i think professor leiton was around about the same time i was obsessed with ace attorney")

6. She frequently dreams about streaming, including interactions with chat. (Verbatim: "i am the kind of person that dreams of streaming okay too too too often i still remember some of them")

7. She enjoys British tea, particularly royal blend black tea served with milk added afterward. (Verbatim: "the one that I had the royal blend that I had I got to add in the the milk afterwards")

8. She loves eating flapjacks made with oats, golden syrup, and butter. (Verbatim: "I love eating flapjacks... oats, oats, oats, and golden syrup and butter")

9. She finds it difficult to be patient when hungry in formal settings, such as afternoon tea. (Verbatim: "stomach rumbling like mouths salivating just looking at the sandwich like shush sir i'm so hungry please can you finish your story so i can eat this sandwich")

10. She is amused by wordplay and linguistic confusion, as shown by her reaction to the "silent C" joke. (Verbatim: "you're all like gaslighting me into being like no it's silent it's pronounced towels and i was like no it's tacos tacos") [end of text]



1. She is a British VTuber. (Verbatim: "My name is Elia Solari, a British VTuber.")
2. She has been medically diagnosed with agoraphobia. (Verbatim: "I officially was properly medically diagnosed with agoraphobia.")
3. She struggled with being a shut-in and underwent therapy to help her go outside. (Verbatim: "I was like a shut-in like a straight up shut-in and then I had to go to therapy to like help me go back outside.")
4. She identifies as an introvert and needs time alone to recharge. (Verbatim: "as an introvert, I need my time inside to recharge.")
5. She experienced panic attacks when going outside in the past. (Verbatim: "you get like um panic attacks and stuff but I haven't had [one]...")
6. She finds large crowds and social interactions overwhelming and anxiety-inducing. (Verbatim: "I get scared and I'm shy and I'm full of anxiety and a bundle of overthinking brain worm.")
7. She attended Vexpo but felt overwhelmed and socially drained by the end. (Verbatim: "My social battery was like... I'm so deflated. I'm so deflated. My battery be deaded.")
8. She once signed her own standee at an event, jokingly calling it a crime. (Verbatim: "I graffitied my own standee with my signature. That is a crime.")
9. She plays League of Legends and Teamfight Tactics (TFT). (Verbatim: "Do you think they'd let me play League or TFT? If I was in jail?")
10. She jokes about being bad at committing crimes and would do poorly in jail. (Verbatim: "Also bad at committing crimes, which is funny because that is a way of being bad.") [end of text]



1. Elia Stellaria is a British VTuber. (Verbatim: "i am elia stelaria british vtuber got partnered today")

2. She has Irish heritage through her family. (Verbatim: "my british family actually descend from ireland i'll have you now")

3. She survived three months in a remote jungle, which was part of a scientific research expedition. (Verbatim: "anyone who survived three months in the jungle is cool in my book... i had my scientific research permit to be there along with the other people")

4. She is not an outdoor person and found the jungle experience surprising due to her anxieties, though remote areas helped reduce social anxiety. (Verbatim: "I'm surprised I survived because my goodness I'm not an outdoor person... in terms of my anxieties it's actually quite fine")

5. During her jungle expedition, she had to hide from poachers, whom she considered the most dangerous threat. (Verbatim: "if you see anyone else that means they're a poacher... that is the most terrifying threat in the jungle people")

6. She once took a stick from poachers during the expedition and still fondly remembers it. (Verbatim: "but i stole their sticks so you know... it was a good stick it's a very very good stick")

7. Her debut as Elia Stellaria in her current model is the version she chooses to celebrate, not her initial debut with a temporary model. (Verbatim: "for me i don't really want to celebrate that because that was just a time of a lot of tears and a lot of not sleeping... i just want to consider the time from you know when i actually debuted as elia in this model")

8. She associates her early days as a VTuber with significant emotional struggle, including lack of sleep and stress. (Verbatim: "that was just a time of a lot of tears and a lot of not sleeping and a lot of struggle")

9. She owns a standee of herself that features wings, making it wide. (Verbatim: "oh but my standees my standee was super wide because of my wings")

10. She has never been punched in her life and speculates it might feel like being hit in the face with a football. (Verbatim: "fun fact i've never been punched in my life yippee i wonder what it feels like i imagine it feels exactly the same as getting hit in the face of a football") [end of text]



1. She has a physical trait where her knees turn inward due to shorter ligaments in the lower leg. (Verbatim: "the ligaments in the bottom half of my leg are too short so my knees do go inwards")

2. She identifies as British and mentions the cultural habit of not pronouncing the 't' in words. (Verbatim: "cuz i'm british we don't like to pronounce the t's so it's you hecking what mate")

3. She expresses a desire to be associated with Gandalf from *The Lord of the Rings*, citing shared traits like timing and love for fireworks. (Verbatim: "i think i'm more like gandalf because i'm never early or late i arrive precisely when i mean to")

4. She does not have a beard and has no plans to get one, joking that it wouldn’t suit her. (Verbatim: "no beard though actually i feel like it'd be would i be able to suit a beard no i can't be bothered")

5. She humorously claims not to have ears and suggests her buns might be antennae for alien communication, implying fictional or whimsical lore. (Verbatim: "i don't have any ears just to just to clarify... they're actually my antenna to communicate with the with the with i've said too much")

6. She wishes she had joined the VTubing scene sooner, indicating a desire to have started her journey earlier. (Verbatim: "i could only wish i joined sooner")

7. She is able to stream full-time as a VTuber thanks to her audience's support. (Verbatim: "i'm able to do this full time because of you guys")

8. She refers to her streaming as a "superpower" to make people smile, highlighting her goal of bringing happiness. (Verbatim: "i'm here to try and make people smile with my yap like a superpower")

9. She enjoys playing *League of Legends* and *Teamfight Tactics*. (Verbatim: "i just like to play league of legends and team fight tactics")

10. She jokes about becoming a magical anime girl with a wish, but prioritizes simple desires like a chicken burger over transformative powers. (Verbatim: "maybe i can ask for like a chicken burger or something yeah i think that'll be a good enough wish") [end of text]



1. She is British and grew up with a culture of self-deprecation. (Verbatim: "um yes believe in myself more i love the assumption that i believe in myself at all um but i'm british so self-deprecation is just i'm just very good at it's actually something we're raised to do here")

2. She has free healthcare because she lives in England. (Verbatim: "I have free healthcare. I'm in England. I don't need to pay for healthcare here, okay?")

3. Her favorite game is Teamfight Tactics (TFT), and she has a strong passion for it. (Verbatim: "i think i can do it like i actually think i can let's just say once upon a time in a dream before my last dream i i was very obsessed with team fight tactics and did want to be a professional and did do a lot")

4. She once considered pursuing a professional career in Teamfight Tactics. (Verbatim: "i was very obsessed with team fight tactics and did want to be a professional and did do a lot and and thus um yeah")

5. She expresses a desire to do more events like VEXPO in the future. (Verbatim: "i want to do more i want to do more so much more i had an amazing time and it was totally worth traveling out for")

6. She jokes about being lonely and never having had a romantic partner. (Verbatim: "i'm lonely and never experienced that i need a hug a hug hug oh yeah to be my virtual partner for legal reasons this is a joke")

7. She identifies with a "goose goddess" persona humorously, though she denies it being a cult. (Verbatim: "great goose goddess here our cold feathered queen we honor all wings of wisdom" and "not a cult not a cult not a cult not a cult")

8. She has a tendency to get very excited and energetic during streams, sometimes finding herself annoying. (Verbatim: "sometimes i do streams where it's all eppie voice to be honest sometimes the problem is i just get very excited because you guys make me really happy and then when i get really happy i get really hyped and then when i'm really hyped i get really annoying")

9. She uses her voice as a bedtime story for viewers to help them sleep. (Verbatim: "story reading and played every night when i go to bed i hope it helps people fall asleep hopefully if it doesn't then i got nothing that's like the best bedtime story in the universe")

10. She does not believe in herself strongly, attributing it to her British upbringing. (Verbatim: "i love the assumption that i believe in myself at all um but i'm british so self-deprecation is just i'm just very good at it") [end of text]



1. She is planning to develop new outfits, a 3D model, and original songs for her channel. (Verbatim: "Um, for example, you know, new outfits, 3D model, um, original songs, um, all sorts, all sorts, all sorts.")

2. She owns a belt with a heart-shaped buckle that she finds cute. (Verbatim: "Actually, I do have a really cute belt. I have this belt that's got like a little heart-shaped buckle.")

3. She is extremely dedicated to her community and has no plans to leave or graduate from being a VTuber. (Verbatim: "I have no plans to leave or anything of the sort, okay? Don't worry, don't worry.")

4. She refers to herself as being "down bad" for her fans and deeply invested in her channel. (Verbatim: "I'm too down bad for you guys, okay? I have too much planned.")

5. She aspires to attend Vexpo again next year and perform on a bigger scale than before. (Verbatim: "Yeah, I definitely want to be at Vexpo. I definitely want to be at Vexpo next year for sure, for sure, for sure... even bigger than I was this year.")

6. She plans to host a digital meet-and-greet at San Japan in Texas, USA. (Verbatim: "I'll be doing a digital meet and greet on the sunday... at san japan yeah... it's in texas.")

