10. She identifies as British and recently hosted a British-themed meet-and-greet. (Verbatim: "i'm british though do i have to go to i was just doing a british meet and greet like two days ago two three days ago like three days ago") [end of text]



1. She considers "yapping" with her audience to be one of her favorite activities. (Verbatim: "i always wanted to yap and it was like just do what you enjoy and i'm like i enjoy yapping with you guys so big yeah big big")

2. She does not like saying goodbye and prefers "see you later" over "bye-bye". (Verbatim: "i don't i don't i don't like bye-byes bye-byes suck okay bye-byes suck don't like bye-byes")

3. She once created a school project about a fictional space trip to Jupiter during science week. (Verbatim: "when i was in school we had like science week and in science week i had to come up with with my own space trip to to to a planet... and i made a trip to jupiter")

4. In her school project, she set the price for the trip to Jupiter at five pounds, believing it was a high amount. (Verbatim: "the trip was five pounds i was like yes this this is a good amount five pounds that's that's an absolute that snaps that's so much")

5. She is open to fans using her voice clips if done in a funny and non-malicious way. (Verbatim: "as long as it's used in a funny non-malicious manner and it say so that'd be good")

6. She humorously imagines flying to Jupiter on a magical banana. (Verbatim: "you know like i must fly away on my magical banana to jupiter")

7. She mentions needing a shower after streaming, implying a post-stream routine. (Verbatim: "i need a shower um yeah yeah yeah yeah okay okay")

8. She plans to research Team Fight Tactics, indicating interest in the game. (Verbatim: "i'm gonna go research tft and go shower now yay")

9. She expresses appreciation for being remembered during her weekend absence. (Verbatim: "thank you for not forgetting me while i was away for the weekend for vexbo")

10. She frequently uses the phrase "arigato" and "daisuki", showing affection toward her audience. (Verbatim: "arigato arigato da isuki tayo") [end of text]



1. She is British. (Verbatim: "my biggest fault is being british and smelly")
